Relationship to KIPET
---------------------

kipetax is an independent reimplementation, inspired by KIPET, the Kinetic
Parameter Estimation Toolkit:

    https://github.com/kwmcbride/KIPET

KIPET was developed by Kevin McBride, Christina Schenk, Michael Short,
Jose Santiago Rodriguez, David M. Thierry, Salvador Garcia-Munoz and
Lorenz T. Biegler, and is distributed under the GNU General Public License,
version 3.

kipetax contains no source code from KIPET. Its numerical core (discopt
collocation, POUNCE-based NLP solves and covariance, variable projection,
JAX-differentiable shooting) was written from scratch. To make migration
easy, kipetax deliberately follows KIPET's user-facing interface: the
ReactionModel method names and keyword arguments (parameter, component,
state, add_ode, add_data, set_time, simulate, run_opt, ...) and the
single-letter naming of result tables (Z, X, Y, S, P, ...). These interface
conventions are reused for compatibility only.

If you use kipetax, please also cite the KIPET papers that introduced the
methods and interface it builds on:

  C. Schenk, M. Short, J.S. Rodriguez, D. Thierry, L.T. Biegler,
  S. Garcia-Munoz, W. Chen. Introducing KIPET: A novel open-source software
  package for kinetic parameter estimation from experimental datasets
  including spectra. Computers & Chemical Engineering 134 (2020) 106716.
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compchemeng.2019.106716

  M. Short, L.T. Biegler, S. Garcia-Munoz, W. Chen. Estimating variances and
  kinetic parameters from spectra across multiple datasets using KIPET.
  Chemometrics and Intelligent Laboratory Systems 203 (2020) 104012.
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chemolab.2020.104012

